/**
 * @defgroup StarVMCApplication StarVMCApplication — STAR VMC Application Layer
 * @brief Production TVirtualMCApplication with hit collection, particle
 *        stack, primary generators, and g2t table infrastructure.
 *
 * StarVMCApplication provides the full VMC application stack used by STAR
 * for GEANT3-based detector simulation:
 * - StarVMCApplication: the TVirtualMCApplication singleton that drives
 *   the simulation lifecycle and connects primary generation, field, and
 *   stepping to the hit-collection machinery.
 * - StarMCStack: particle-lineage stack implementing TVirtualMCStack.
 * - StarMCHit / StarMCHits / StarMCHitCollection: per-step hit data
 *   structures and the singleton manager that routes steps to g2t tables.
 * - StarMCParticle: TObject wrapper adding mother-daughter references to
 *   TParticle.
 * - StarMCPrimaryGenerator hierarchy: abstract base plus four concrete
 *   implementations (simple phase-space, ROOT file, HBOOK file).
 * - St_g2t_Chair hierarchy: per-detector TChair subclasses that write
 *   rows into the g2t hit tables (TPC, SVT, SSD, EMC, TOF, etc.).
 * - StHitDescriptor: aggregate binding detector metadata to its chair.
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @class StarVMCApplication
 * @brief Production STAR TVirtualMCApplication.
 *
 * Singleton (accessed via Instance()) that owns StarMCStack,
 * StarMCPrimaryGenerator, StarMagField, and StarMCHits.  InitMC() loads an
 * optional ROOT config macro then calls gMC->SetStack / Init /
 * BuildPhysics.  RunMC(n) calls gMC->ProcessRun(n).  ConstructGeometry()
 * calls gMC->SetRootGeometry().  InitGeometry() prints material/medium
 * tables and initialises the hit descriptors.  Stepping() delegates to
 * fMcHits->Step().  PostTrack() releases secondary StarMCParticle memory.
 * FinishEvent() finalises g2t tables via fMcHits->FinishEvent().
 * Field() delegates to StarMagField or falls back to a uniform 5 kG z-field.
 */

/**
 * @class StarMCStack
 * @brief STAR TVirtualMCStack with particle-lineage support.
 *
 * Dual-container design: a TObjArray of all StarMCParticle objects ever
 * created in the event (for parent-daughter navigation), plus a
 * std::stack<StarMCParticle*> for tracks pending transport.  PushTrack()
 * builds the mother-daughter TRef chain and applies a rapidity cut
 * |pz/e| < tanh(6.3).  Reset() clears the event.  SetNprimary() allows
 * generators to set the primary count directly.  GetParticles() exposes
 * the full TObjArray for PostTrack() cleanup.
 */

/**
 * @class StarMCHit
 * @brief Per-step MC hit record with full entry/exit geometry.
 *
 * TDataSet-derived.  Stores TLorentzVector positions at entry, current
 * step, and exit in both global and local TGeo frames.  Tracks cumulative
 * step length and energy deposition.  The volume-path array (TArrayS,
 * depth 16) encodes the TGeo node-path indices for routing to the
 * correct St_g2t_Chair.  setEntry()/setExit() snapshot positions.
 * getLocal(TGeoHMatrix*) transforms the current global position to the
 * local detector frame.
 */

/**
 * @class StarMCHits
 * @brief Singleton hit-collection manager and g2t table router.
 *
 * Created once via StarMCHits::instance().  Init() reads detector
 * descriptors (St_det_user, St_det_path, St_det_hit tables) from the
 * dataset tree and builds per-volume StHitDescriptor/St_g2t_Chair pairs.
 * InitLegacy() uses a compiled-in Detector_G2T_t table instead.
 * Step() is called at each VMC step: it identifies the current detector
 * from the TGeo volume ID, fills the GHit_t accumulator, and calls
 * FillG2Table() which dispatches to St_g2t_Chair::Fill().
 * FinishEvent() writes the g2t_event, g2t_track, g2t_vertex, and
 * g2t_gepart tables from the stack.  NewTable() and NewChair() are static
 * factories for creating g2t table and chair objects by type name.
 */

/**
 * @class StarMCHitCollection
 * @brief TObjArray of StarMCHit objects with a Count() accessor.
 */

/**
 * @class StarMCParticle
 * @brief TObject wrapping TParticle with parent-daughter TRef links.
 *
 * Stores a stack index (fID), a generator-list index (fIdGen), an owned
 * TParticle*, a TRef to the mother StarMCParticle, and a TRefArray of
 * daughters.  Print() displays track ID, PDG identity, mother name, and
 * daughter count.  PrintDaughters() recursively prints the daughter list.
 */

/**
 * @class StarMCPrimaryGenerator
 * @brief Abstract base class for STAR primary-particle generators.
 *
 * Holds TVirtualMCStack*, origin TVector3, primary count, particle ID,
 * and an option string.  Subclasses override GeneratePrimaries() (no-arg
 * form) and GeneratePrimaries(const TVector3&) to push particles onto the
 * stack.  A static Instance() pointer is set in the constructor so any
 * code can reach the active generator.
 */

/**
 * @class StarMCSimplePrimaryGenerator
 * @brief Uniform-phase-space primary generator.
 *
 * Generates fNofPrimaries particles per event uniformly sampled in pT,
 * eta, phi, and z-vertex ranges.  Accepts parameters via a constructor,
 * a text-file constructor (whitespace-delimited parameter file), or
 * SetGenerator().  Particle species may be given as a GEANT3 code
 * (option="G") or PDG code.  GeneratePrimaries(const TVector3&) pushes all
 * primaries at the supplied vertex.
 */

/**
 * @class StarMCRootPrimaryGenerator
 * @brief Reads primary particles from a ROOT TTree in HEPEVT format.
 *
 * Opens a ROOT file, locates the tree named h<HbtId>, and reads one full
 * HepEvent per GeneratePrimaries() call.  Reconstructs the mother-daughter
 * topology.  Particles with known PDG codes are pushed onto the VMC stack;
 * particles with daughters or status >= 2 are pushed with toBeDone=0.
 * If a TDataSet was supplied, writes the HEPEVT header and per-particle
 * rows into an St_particle table.
 */

/**
 * @class StarMCHBPrimaryGenerator
 * @brief Reads primaries from an HBOOK-converted ROOT TTree (HBT format).
 *
 * Identical logic to StarMCRootPrimaryGenerator but reads from an HBOOK-
 * converted ROOT file.  Vertex coordinates are converted from mm to cm;
 * time-of-flight is converted from mm/s to cm/s units.  Tree name is
 * h<HbtId>.
 */

/**
 * @class St_g2t_Chair
 * @brief Abstract TChair base for all STAR g2t hit-table accessors.
 *
 * Declares the virtual interface Fill(GHit_t&) used by StarMCHits to
 * write one hit row per simulation step, plus positional accessors
 * (GetX/Y/Z, DetectorId, Sector, PadRow, TrackId, HitPosition).
 * Concrete subclasses — St_g2t_ctf_hitC, St_g2t_emc_hitC,
 * St_g2t_fgt_hitC, St_g2t_fst_hitC, St_g2t_ftp_hitC, St_g2t_ist_hitC,
 * St_g2t_mwc_hitC, St_g2t_pix_hitC, St_g2t_pmd_hitC, St_g2t_rch_hitC,
 * St_g2t_ssd_hitC, St_g2t_svt_hitC, St_g2t_tpc_hitC, St_g2t_vpd_hitC —
 * implement Fill() for each STAR detector system.
 */

/**
 * @class StHitDescriptor
 * @brief Aggregate binding detector metadata to its g2t chair.
 *
 * TNamed subclass used by StarMCHits to route a VMC step to the correct
 * g2t table.  Holds a TDataSet* detector node, St_det_user* user-parameter
 * table, St_det_path* sensitive-volume path table, St_det_hit* hit-format
 * descriptor, an St_g2t_Chair*, and a volume-level count fNVL.
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
